  "implemented": [
    "Captured host-neutral CLI manager, actual three CLI stores and physical file/probe owners are registered for shutdown and raw drain before profile release. Constructor-selected paths/environment and separate current CLI/read/write/probe/reference grants remain outside RPC.",
    "CLI files have bounded actual no-follow FD reads, aggregate preflight, fresh physical/byte receipts, exclusive verified/fsynced publication, retained failed-close receipts, and conservative preservation of unknown bytes. Syntax edits retain comments/unknown sections and exact saved credential strings.",
    "Actual AgentManager configuration/admission leases refuse affected live/cached sessions and queued/admitted/raw starts. Raw filesystem and real SDK refresh acknowledgements remain owned. Potentially published rejection leaves a failed-backend fence until explicit successful retry; cached adapters lacking a real refresh capability refuse before effects.",
    "Probe grants, original environment source names, resolved actual transport input and configuration bindings are checked before each effect. Supplied stale MCP fingerprints refuse before contact. Portable probes use literal command vectors, no implicit task token or redirects, and join real child/HTTP cleanup without replay.",
    "Portable snapshots mask configured credential values and private URL parameters; unsupported URL edits refuse before publication. Prototype names normalized by upsert are refused before borrowing the mutation lease. Missing markers cannot silently erase saved values.",
    "Task images use captured attachment-root receipts and ordinary task metadata/event flow. Atomic no-replace publication follows actual fsync/FD close. Precommit failure rolls back only provably owned bytes; accepted DB/files survive late caller loss. Pending handles/retirement receipts fence ordinary task deletion and keep the protected profile until explicit cleanup retry.",
    "Eight exact commands traverse actual singleton dispatch, explicit native facade and complementary Rust DTOs. The golden corpus contains 446 actual TypeScript requests; native validation also consumes eight actual singleton responses, including a loopback MCP handshake and physical persisted image bytes.",
    "Local OAuth tests select finite isolated real listener ports and exercise cancelled startup, failed bind and acknowledged close without assuming port 3000 is free. The production default remains ports 3000 through 3010."
  ],
